<title>CHINA: China's foreign exchange market closed.</title>
<headline>China's foreign exchange market closed.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-01-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai-based interbank foreign exchange market, the China Foreign Exchange Trade System, was closed on Wednesday for the New Year holiday and trading will resume on Thursday.</p>
<p>In the last trading session of 1996 on Tuesday, the Chinese yuan closed up at 8.2982 against the U.S. dollar.</p>
</text>
